TASK CHORE58
	TITLE "investigate running awawa in CI, and what it would simplify"
	STATUS draft
	DESC "Raised in the review of pull request 101: the guards CI job does not install awawa, so"
		+ "check:anchors parses the corpus text itself; find out whether awawa can run in CI and"
		+ "what it would simplify or add"
	SPEC "the task records whether awawa can be installed in a GitHub Actions runner, from which"
		+ "source and at which cost per run"
	SPEC "the task records, for each place named in its rationale, the lines awawa in CI would"
		+ "remove or the check it would add, and whether that gain is worth the installation"
	SPEC "when the gain is worth it, a todo task carries the change; otherwise the reason is"
		+ "written in this task"
	RATIONALE "awawa is today a local x86-64 binary, 2.7.0 in ~/.local/bin, and the repository"
		+ "names no source to install it from; it could simplify the corpus parser of"
		+ "scripts/check-corpus-anchors.ts and its spec, which awawa show or status --json would"
		+ "replace, and the whole guard if lint L016 consulted git instead of the disk; it would"
		+ "add a CI run of awawa fmt --check and awawa lint --strict, which no job runs today, so"
		+ "the conformance of the corpus is checked only on the machine of its author"

