TASK FEAT80
	TITLE "Repair a rejected save from the save manager"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "loading a save the validator rejects shows, besides its errors, the defects grouped by"
		+ "kind with the fix proposed for each; a fix that can be left out carries a box to tick,"
		+ "and a fix any rewritten file carries is shown as always applied, with what it discards"
	SPEC "a defect for which no fix is proposed is shown as such, with the entry it concerns and no"
		+ "box"
	SPEC "confirming downloads a new file under a name distinct from the loaded one, and shows what"
		+ "the validator still reports about it"
	SPEC "a save whose section count is unsupported shows the one defect it produces and no repair"
		+ "to confirm"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT79
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT70
	WAVE 7
	RATIONALE "Today a rejected save ends the page: the route shows the list of validation messages"
		+ "and nothing else, and the visualization area stays empty. The repair view takes that"
		+ "dead end and turns it into the table the user acts on, reusing the export path the wave"
		+ "before builds so that the corrected save leaves as a new file and the loaded one is"
		+ "never overwritten. Grouping by kind is what makes the table usable when a defect repeats"
		+ "across hundreds of entries. A fix the rewrite itself carries cannot be left out, the"
		+ "parser having already dropped the unreadable line and the serializer writing the float"
		+ "suffix back, so it is shown as always applied with the loss named in its row rather than"
		+ "behind a box that could not be honoured, because a save manager that silently drops"
		+ "entries of a save is the failure this feature exists to avoid. A call that does not"
		+ "complete keeps the one failure idiom of the package, distinct from what the validator"
		+ "reports"
		REF @DECISION.UiSaveManagerHasOneUiErrorIdiom
		REF @DECISION.ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
		REF @DECISION.AGuardRefusesLocatorsTheScreenDoesNotShow
		REF @TASK.FEAT79
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-21 on pull request #108: the defects are presented as a table of"
		+ "the fixes to apply, ideally with a box per fix, and confirming creates a new corrected"
		+ "save file"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Read on 2026-09-21 on the default branch: the display route renders the validation"
		+ "messages and the visualization area is shown only when the save carries no error, and"
		+ "the merge result is the only place that turns serialized content into a downloadable"
		+ "file"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager

TASK TEST81
	TITLE "Repair a corrupted scenario fixture in the save manager"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "a scenario fixture is generated carrying a float gauge written without its decimal suffix"
		+ "and an unreadable entry line, and the validator rejects it"
	SPEC "the save manager shows that fixture as repairable, and confirming yields a file the"
		+ "validator accepts"
	SPEC "a scenario fixture is generated whose section count is unsupported, and the save manager"
		+ "shows it as not repairable"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT80
	WAVE 7
	RATIONALE "The repair is a flow across three engines, files, blobs and downloads, where the"
		+ "package has no layer below end to end; the scenario is what covers it. The fixtures are"
		+ "declared in the generator and replayed byte for byte by the guard, never copied from a"
		+ "real save, so no real player name and no real Steam account identifier reaches them and"
		+ "the corruption they carry is built on purpose rather than found. Two fixtures are needed"
		+ "because the two outcomes of the feature are opposite: one save that the round trip mends"
		+ "entirely, one whose section count hides everything else. The scenario asserts what the"
		+ "screen shows, the presence and the location of what is offered, never the sentence a"
		+ "rule produced, and it changes the UI for nothing but its own sake"
		REF @DECISION.ScenarioFixturesAreGeneratedAndReplayedByAGuard
		REF @DECISION.AUiScenarioAssertsWhatTheScreenShows
		REF @DECISION.UiSaveManagerHasNoComponentTestLayer
		REF @DECISION.NoRealPlayerNameInPublicContent
		REF @PROCESS.ATestTaskChangesTheUiOnlyForItsOwnSake
		REF @TASK.FEAT80
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-21 on pull request #108: the wave delivers a repair the user"
		+ "confirms, so the scenario covers the confirmation and the file it produces"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Read on 2026-09-21 on the default branch: the four scenario fixtures of the package are"
		+ "generated by the fixture script and replayed by the guard, and the invalid one carries a"
		+ "single violation on one record"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager

TASK FEAT82
	TITLE "Detect the links between the objects of a save that lead nowhere"
	STATUS draft
	WAVE 7
	DESC "drafted for memory, no research done: which links a save carries, which of them the game"
		+ "tolerates broken and what fix each defect calls for are established when the task is"
		+ "refined"
	SPEC "a link from one object of a save to another that names an identifier nothing carries is"
		+ "reported by the validator with the entry it sits in, the equipment identifier of a"
		+ "player naming no inventory being the first case"
	SPEC "each defect so reported enters the repair plan, with a fix or as not repairable"
		+ "automatically"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT80
	RATIONALE "The validator checks each entry against the schema of its section and never one"
		+ "entry against another, so a save whose player names an equipment inventory that does not"
		+ "exist is accepted today. The owner expects the repair to earn its keep on the coherence"
		+ "of the data rather than on its shape, in a second step once the minimal repair of wave 7"
		+ "is delivered. The check enters the single validator, which changes the verdict of the"
		+ "display, merge and validate flows for a save accepted today, a cost to weigh at"
		+ "refinement. A repeated identifier is no such defect, the game itself writing collisions"
		+ "between inventories and world objects; a link that leads nowhere is"
		REF @DECISION.ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
		REF @RULE.IdentifiersAreSharedByInventoriesAndWorldObjects
		REF @SECTION.Players
		REF @SECTION.Inventories
		REF @TASK.FEAT78
	SOURCE "Owner ruling of 2026-09-21 on the rewrite of the wave 7 tasks of pull request 108: the"
		+ "validator validates against a schema, the least a save fixer adds is checking the links"
		+ "between objects, an equipment identifier having to name an inventory; that part comes in"
		+ "a second step and is drafted for memory only, without further research"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

