TASK DOCS86
	TITLE "Type the era of a rule and a section by game release"
	STATUS implemented
	DELIVERED_BY 115
	WAVE 5
	DESC "The decisions taken here must anticipate the next tasks of wave 5 and especially"
		+ "@TASK.FEAT68"
		REF @TASK.FEAT68
	SPEC "the eras current, legacy and both are dropped: no value of HOLDS_FOR names an era"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::FIELD HOLDS_FOR @GAME_RELEASE"
	SPEC "HOLDS_FOR names a GAME_RELEASE and is repeatable: a rule or a section holds for each"
		+ "release it names, and for no other; HOLDS_FOR all, alone, marks a statement that does"
		+ "not depend on the release"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::a release the statement holds for"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::all, alone: the statement does not depend on the release"
	SPEC "HOLDS_FOR names only a release that creates a branch in the code, one the code tells"
		+ "apart from the release before it; a release the code does not tell apart is never named,"
		+ "and a save it writes is read by the branch of the last named release before it"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::named only if the code tells it apart from the"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/normalizeRawSections.js::rawParts.length ==="
			+ "LEGACY_SPLIT_PARTS_COUNT"
	SPEC "each entity that carried an era is rewritten with the releases it holds for, read from"
		+ "the branches of the code and not translated from the era it carried"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-specification/sections.awawa"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-specification/rules.awawa"
	SPEC "the fields and constraints the schema keys on the era, INDEX, LEGACY_INDEX and the"
		+ "incoming CONSTRAINED_BY of a section, are keyed on the releases instead, so that a"
		+ "section written by the latest release still needs a rule that cites it"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::the position of the section in the format 2.004 and later"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::the position of the section in the format 1.618 and earlier"
	SPEC "the decision that cites a game release as a source is rewritten in place: its SPEC that"
		+ "no type of the specification area carries the game version as a field of its own, and"
		+ "its REJECTED version field on RULE, are revised to admit the release a statement holds"
		+ "for, the previous form kept as a REJECTED"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/decisions.awawa::DECISION AGameReleaseIsCitedAsASource"
	SPEC "the decision that the era is not the archive is rewritten to name a section the game"
		+ "stopped writing by the releases it holds for instead of HOLDS_FOR legacy"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/decisions.awawa::DECISION TheEraIsNotTheArchive"
	SPEC "the ruling that a save is never discriminated by its declared version alone is recorded,"
		+ "and the cross-check of a save against its version is a draft task of wave 5"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/decisions.awawa::DECISION"
			+ "ASaveIsNeverDiscriminatedByItsVersionAlone"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/tasks.awawa::TASK FEAT89"
	RATIONALE "HOLDS_FOR current|legacy|both assumes two formats, split by the removal of the"
		+ "Terrain Layers section; the project now handles more, and a two-valued era cannot say"
		+ "that a statement holds since 2.102 only. The eras are not mapped onto sets of releases:"
		+ "that mapping would carry the two-format assumption into the new field. Naming only the"
		+ "releases that create a branch in the code keeps the list short and stable: a patch such"
		+ "as 2.103, which changes no save key, adds no value and touches no entity, which answers"
		+ "the objection that a closed list must grow with every release. The change conflicts with"
		+ "a recorded decision, which rejects the game version as a field of the specification area"
		+ "on the ground that it would mean the version of the last reading; typed by release, the"
		+ "field names the releases the statement holds for, not the one it was read in"
		REF @DECISION.AGameReleaseIsCitedAsASource
		REF @DECISION.TheEraIsNotTheArchive
		REF @FIELDSET.ReleaseScope
		REF @SCHEMA.SECTION
		REF @GAME_RELEASE.1.618
		REF @GAME_RELEASE.2.008
		REF @GAME_RELEASE.2.102
		REF @GAME_RELEASE.2.103
		REF @TASK.FEAT55
	SOURCE "Review of pull request 111 by the owner, 2026-09-22: HOLDS_FOR should be typed by game"
		+ "release and repeatable; legacy no longer suffices now that more than two releases are"
		+ "handled; deferred to a task of wave 5"
		PR 111
	SOURCE "Clarification by the owner on pull request 111, 2026-09-22: legacy, current and both"
		+ "are dropped in favour of game releases, and HOLDS_FOR lists only the game releases that"
		+ "create a branch in the code"
		PR 111
	SOURCE "The owner on pull request 115, 2026-09-22: a rule that holds whatever the release"
		+ "carries HOLDS_FOR all"
		PR 115

